The generated vertex shader runs max_primitives * verts_per_prim times per
mesh workgroup, whatever the mesh shader's primitive count, and loaded the
whole vertex and primitive record even for corners whose primitive is past
the count or culled, only to overwrite the position. Branch around the
fetches and write only the clip position for dead corners.

Position is written through the same variable on both paths, so a mesh
shader without a position output keeps the constant position.

Whether this wins depends on how many corners are dead and on how well the
branch behaves on Adreno; measure with a low-occupancy workload (meshlets
with far fewer than max_primitives primitives) and one with none dead, and
drop this commit if the second regresses. Not compiled or run here. Dead
points keep an undefined point size; they are clipped by position.
